From 4d3290ea56de00410f466a41090882ef240736e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:27:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] JOY Bus: the adapter thread gives a room the owner's replies
 itself

Replies to a room used to go out when the owner's emulation next collected them, so an owner
held up by anything (waiting on another machine, the pad sync) held its replies back and the
others waited for them. The adapter thread now sends each reply the moment it is in, in the
order of the line; commands that are not sent (idle status polls held back, a GBA that is not
there) keep their place in the line as placeholders. Solo play is unchanged.
---
